  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "One hot topic with VRChat right now is that since anyone can set arbitrary thumbnails it's possible to be deceptive about the contents of a world. Other platforms have solved this issue by automatically taking a 360° screenshot from spawn upon upload. This idea could be tweaked to work with VRChat, and as an added bonus since it's a cubemap a more dynamic and interactive image viewer could easily be added for this special thumbnail. \n\nHaving this be a built in SDK feature and withholding the ability to upload a custom image for this thumbnail would reduce the potential for abuse. It wouldn't eliminate it, but it would make it more difficult.",
